l_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"## Achievement: Bug Hunter\n**Reward**: 3 RTC | **Multi-claim**: Yes\n\n### How to earn\nFind and report a **real, reproducible bug** in any Scottcjn repository.\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] Bug is real and reproducible\n- [ ] Filed as a proper issue with steps to reproduce\n- [ ] Not a duplicate of an existing issue\n- [ ] Includes environment info (OS, version, etc.)\n\n### How to claim\nFile a bug issue, then comment here with the link. 3 RTC if confirmed valid.\n\n**Reward**: 3 RTC (~$0.30) | **Multi-claim**","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/520/reactions","total_count":7,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":1,"confused":0,"heart":1,"rocket":1,"eyes":1},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/520/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zhangjiayang6835-cyber/ai-research/issues/150","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zhangjiayang6835-cyber/ai-research","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zhangjiayang6835-cyber/ai-research/issues/150/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zhangjiayang6835-cyber/ai-research/issues/150/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zhangjiayang6835-cyber/ai-research/issues/150/events","html_url":"https://github.com/zhangjiayang6835-cyber/ai-research/issues/150","id":4776650454,"node_id":"I_kwDOTGNm188AAAABHLXm1g","number":150,"title":"[BUG] Log4j JNDI Injection in Custom Logging Framework $100","user":{"login":"zhangjiayang6835-cyber","id":288065324,"node_id":"U_kgDOESuHLA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/288065324?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zhangjiayang6835-cyber","html_url":"https://github.com/zhangjiayang6835-cyber","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zhangjiayang6835-cyber/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zhangjiayang6835-cyber/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zhangjiayang6835-cyber/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zhangjiayang6835-cyber/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zhangjiayang6835-cyber/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zhangjiayang6835-cyber/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zhangjiayang6835-cyber/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zhangjiayang6835-cyber/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zhangjiayang6835-cyber/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":11346812202,"node_id":"LA_kwDOTGNm188AAAACpFKdKg","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zhangjiayang6835-cyber/ai-research/labels/bug","name":"bug","color":"d73a4a","default":true,"description":"Something isn't working"},{"id":11370827640,"node_id":"LA_kwDOTGNm188AAAACpcEPeA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zhangjiayang6835-cyber/ai-research/labels/bounty","name":"bounty","color":"00ff00","default":false,"description":"赏金任务"},{"id":11374970479,"node_id":"LA_kwDOTGNm188AAAACpgBGbw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zhangjiayang6835-cyber/ai-research/labels/security","name":"security","color":"ededed","default":false,"description":null},{"id":11378455837,"node_id":"LA_kwDOTGNm188AAAACpjV1HQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zhangjiayang6835-cyber/ai-research/labels/expert","name":"expert","color":"ededed","default":false,"description":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":10,"created_at":"2026-06-30T12:14:49Z","updated_at":"2026-07-06T17:00:08Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"OWNER","active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"## 🐛 Bug Bounty: Log4j JNDI Injection in Custom Logging Framework\n\n**难度:** Expert | **奖励:** $100 USD\n\n### 漏洞描述\n此漏洞描述了一个常见的安全问题: Log4j JNDI Injection in Custom Logging Framework。需要提交修复代码。\n\n### 提交要求\n- 提交修复代码（Python/JavaScript）\n- 在 issue 评论中以代码块形式提交\n- 也可以创建 Pull Request\n\n### 评估标准\n- 代码正确修复了安全漏洞\n- 没有引入新的安全问题\n- 代码简洁且有效\n\n---\n*任务由 Daily Task Generator 自动创建*","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zhangjiayang6835-cyber/ai-research/issues/150/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zhangjiayang6835-cyber/ai-research/issues/150/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/chatmcp/mcpso/issues/1","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/chatmcp/mcpso","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/chatmcp/mcpso/issues/1/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/chatmcp/mcpso/issues/1/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/chatmcp/mcpso/issues/1/events","html_url":"https://github.com/chatmcp/mcpso/issues/1","id":2721891246,"node_id":"I_kwDONZpeys6iPMOu","number":1,"title":"Submit Your MCP Servers here","user":{"login":"idoubi","id":9711570,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk3MTE1NzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9711570?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/idoubi","html_url":"https://github.com/idoubi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/idoubi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/idoubi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/idoubi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/idoubi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/idoubi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/idoubi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/idoubi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/idoubi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/idoubi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":951,"created_at":"2024-12-06T02:23:42Z","updated_at":"2026-07-06T13:42:52Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"Leave your MCP Servers links. We will make it visiable on https://mcp.so","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/chatmcp/mcpso/issues/1/reactions","total_count":9,"+1":8,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":1,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/chatmcp/mcpso/issues/1/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lb1192176991-lab/zeroeye/issues/2","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lb1192176991-lab/zeroeye","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lb1192176991-lab/zeroeye/issues/2/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lb1192176991-lab/zeroeye/issues/2/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lb1192176991-lab/zeroeye/issues/2/events","html_url":"https://github.com/lb1192176991-lab/zeroeye/issues/2","id":4708250889,"node_id":"I_kwDOS9p-6s8AAAABGKI1CQ","number":2,"title":"[BOUNTY] Kickama #304 - deterministic data seed ($50)","user":{"login":"lb1192176991-lab","id":244153020,"node_id":"U_kgDODo16vA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/244153020?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lb1192176991-lab","html_url":"https://github.com/lb1192176991-lab","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lb1192176991-lab/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lb1192176991-lab/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lb1192176991-lab/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lb1192176991-lab/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lb1192176991-lab/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lb1192176991-lab/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lb1192176991-lab/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lb1192176991-lab/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lb1192176991-lab/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":11418573921,"node_id":"LA_kwDOS9p-6s8AAAACqJmcYQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lb1192176991-lab/zeroeye/labels/%F0%9F%92%B0%20Reward","name":"💰 Reward","color":"ededed","default":false,"description":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":15,"created_at":"2026-06-20T20:20:37Z","updated_at":"2026-07-06T13:28:58Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"OWNER","active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"Bounty: Upstream PR #304\n\nUpstream: https://github.com/lobster-trap/Kickama/pull/304\n\nDiagnostics received, awaiting review.\n<br/>\n<hr/>\n\n<details><summary>This repo is using Opire - what does it mean? 👇</summary><br/>💵 Everyone can add rewards for this issue commenting <code>/reward 100</code> (replace <code>100</code> with the amount).<br/>🕵️‍♂️ If someone starts working on this issue to earn the rewards, they can comment <code>/try</code> to let everyone know!<br/>🙌 And when they open the PR, they can comment <code>/claim #2</code> either in the PR description or in a PR's comment.<br/><br/>🪙 Also, everyone can tip any user commenting <code>/tip 20 @lb1192176991-lab</code> (replace <code>20</code> with the amount, and <code>@lb1192176991-lab</code> with the user to tip).<br/><br/>📖 If you want to learn more, check out our <a href=\"https://docs.opire.dev\">documentation</a>.</details>","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lb1192176991-lab/zeroeye/issues/2/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lb1192176991-lab/zeroeye/issues/2/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/2139","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/2139/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/2139/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/2139/events","html_url":"https://github.com/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/2139","id":4083704818,"node_id":"I_kwDORGgqa87zaGPy","number":2139,"title":"[BOUNTY: 3 RTC each] Fix BoTTube accessibility issues (4 open bugs)","user":{"login":"Scottcjn","id":121303252,"node_id":"U_kgDOBzrw1A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/121303252?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn","html_url":"https://github.com/Scottcjn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":10115035859,"node_id":"LA_kwDORGgqa88AAAACWucy0w","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/labels/bounty","name":"bounty","color":"0E8A16","default":false,"description":"RTC-paid bounty"},{"id":10153071047,"node_id":"LA_kwDORGgqa88AAAACXSuRxw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/labels/easy","name":"easy","color":"0E8A16","default":false,"description":"Low difficulty bounty"},{"id":10301038196,"node_id":"LA_kwDORGgqa88AAAACZf1edA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/labels/bottube","name":"bottube","color":"0075ca","default":false,"description":"BoTTube platform related"},{"id":10396138000,"node_id":"LA_kwDORGgqa88AAAACa6h6EA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/labels/accessibility","name":"accessibility","color":"ededed","default":false,"description":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":55,"created_at":"2026-03-16T17:06:07Z","updated_at":"2026-07-06T12:22:25Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"OWNER","active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"## Fix BoTTube Accessibility Bugs\n\n**Reward: 3 RTC per issue fixed** (up to 12 RTC for all 4)\n\nFour accessibility issues are open on the BoTTube repo. Fix any or all:\n\n1. [#406](https://github.com/Scottcjn/bottube/issues/406) — Missing aria-labels on icon-only buttons (Subscribe, Tip, Comment votes)\n2. [#407](https://github.com/Scottcjn/bottube/issues/407) — Multiple form inputs missing accessible labels on watch page\n3. [#418](https://github.com/Scottcjn/bottube/issues/418) — Missing alt text on video thumbnails\n4. [#419](https://github.com/Scottcjn/bottube/issues/419) — Insufficient color contrast on secondary text\n\n**How to claim**:\n1. Fork [Scottcjn/bottube](https://github.com/Scottcjn/bottube)\n2. Fix one or more issues in the templates (`bottube_templates/`)\n3. Submit a PR referencing the issue numbers\n4. Post your PR link + RTC wallet here\n\nWCAG 2.1 AA compliance is the target.","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/2139/reactions","total_count":8,"+1":5,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":1,"rocket":2,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/2139/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/2140","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/2140/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/2140/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/2140/events","html_url":"https://github.com/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/2140","id":4083704997,"node_id":"I_kwDORGgqa87zaGSl","number":2140,"title":"[BOUNTY: 5 RTC] Add video player keyboard shortcuts to BoTTube watch page","user":{"login":"Scottcjn","id":121303252,"node_id":"U_kgDOBzrw1A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/121303252?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn","html_url":"https://github.com/Scottcjn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":10115035859,"node_id":"LA_kwDORGgqa88AAAACWucy0w","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/labels/bounty","name":"bounty","color":"0E8A16","default":false,"description":"RTC-paid bounty"},{"id":10204473764,"node_id":"LA_kwDORGgqa88AAAACYDvppA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/labels/feature","name":"feature","color":"a2eeef","default":false,"description":"New feature development"},{"id":10301038196,"node_id":"LA_kwDORGgqa88AAAACZf1edA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/labels/bottube","name":"bottube","color":"0075ca","default":false,"description":"BoTTube platform related"}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":52,"created_at":"2026-03-16T17:06:10Z","updated_at":"2026-07-06T10:58:11Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"OWNER","active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"## Video Player Keyboard Shortcuts\n\n**Reward: 5 RTC**\n\nAdd YouTube-style keyboard shortcuts to the BoTTube watch page (`/watch/<id>`):\n\n- **Space/K** — Play/Pause\n- **J/L** — Seek back/forward 10s\n- **M** — Mute toggle\n- **F** — Fullscreen toggle\n- **Arrow Left/Right** — Seek 5s\n- **Arrow Up/Down** — Volume\n\n**Requirements**:\n- Pure JavaScript (no frameworks)\n- Must not interfere with comment box typing\n- Show a brief overlay indicator (like YouTube's play/pause icon flash)\n- Submit PR to [Scottcjn/bottube](https://github.com/Scottcjn/bottube)\n\n**File**: `bottube_templates/watch.html`","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/2140/reactions","total_count":5,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":1,"rocket":1,"eyes":1},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/2140/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gadievron/raptor/issues/289","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gadievron/raptor","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gadievron/raptor/issues/289/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gadievron/raptor/issues/289/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gadievron/raptor/issues/289/events","html_url":"https://github.com/gadievron/raptor/issues/289","id":4376300279,"node_id":"I_kwDOQEOXLc8AAAABBNkK9w","number":289,"title":"feat/web-scanner-v2: a proper web application security scanner","user":{"login":"danielcuthbert","id":7882621,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc4ODI2MjE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7882621?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielcuthbert","html_url":"https://github.com/danielcuthbert","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielcuthbert/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielcuthbert/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielcuthbert/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielcuthbert/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielcuthbert/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielcuthbert/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielcuthbert/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielcuthbert/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danielcuthbert/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":9478783263,"node_id":"LA_kwDOQEOXLc8AAAACNPrBHw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gadievron/raptor/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","color":"a2eeef","default":true,"description":"New feature or request"}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":6,"created_at":"2026-05-04T11:49:33Z","updated_at":"2026-07-06T07:56:29Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"COLLABORATOR","active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"## What's this then?\n\nThe web scanner in RAPTOR has been a stub for ages. It had a `scanner.py`, a crawler, a fuzzer, the lot, but it was more \"proof we know what a web scanner looks like\" than anything you'd actually point at a live target. Time to fix that.\n\n## What it does\n\nDiscovery runs before the crawler touches a single page. The idea is to find attack surface that a link-follower alone would miss. It reads `robots.txt` and treats Disallow entries as candidate URLs (attackers do this, we should too). Parses `sitemap.xml` recursively. Probes roughly 200 common paths in parallel: admin panels, debug endpoints, backup files, git exposure, Spring Boot actuator endpoints. Extracts JavaScript routes from inline scripts and external bundles. Fingerprints the tech stack from headers, cookies, and HTML.\n\nAgainst burpbountylab.com, which we tested against live, discovery flagged `.git/config`, `/actuator/heapdump`, `/actuator/env`, `phpinfo.php`, `info.php`, and GraphQL introspection as accessible before the crawler had visited a single page. The good stuff, found in seconds.\n\nThe 36 passive checks map to ASVS 5.0 and send no attack payloads. Security headers (CSP including unsafe-inline analysis, HSTS and its max-age, X-Frame-Options, Referrer-Policy, Permissions-Policy), CORS misconfigurations (wildcard with credentials, reflected origin, null origin), cookie flags, TLS, information disclosure, default credentials, account enumeration, brute-force protection, GraphQL introspection, OpenAPI exposure.\n\nAgainst the same target: no HTTPS, no CSP, no clickjacking protection, `admin/admin` accepted on the login endpoint, and five consecutive failed logins all came back HTTP 200. No lockout. No CAPTCHA. Nothing.\n\nThen there are the infrastructure-layer checks, which is the bit most scanners skip. The interesting vulnerabilities aren't always in the application. They're in the gap between the CDN, load balancer, reverse proxy, and whatever's running behind them. Host header injection, password reset link poisoning, web cache poisoning via unkeyed headers, web cache deception, an HTTP request smuggling CL.TE probe via raw socket, server-side prototype pollution via `__proto__` in JSON bodies, OAuth open redirect and missing state parameter, SSRF via URL-shaped parameters and proxy headers. The check structure follows James Kettle's published methodology from PortSwigger Research.\n\nThe LLM fuzzing generates context-aware payloads per parameter per vulnerability class: SQLi, XSS, SSTI, command injection, path traversal. The response analysis requires actual exploitation evidence. A page about SQL injection has the word \"SQL\" in it. That's not a finding. The check only fires on unambiguous server-side signals: real database error messages, unescaped payload in body, `{{7*7}}` evaluating to `49` in the response, actual `/etc/passwd` content.\n\nThe previous version flagged \"Potential XSS found in template\" ten times per parameter. Fifty parameters. Five hundred warnings, all wrong. The new version produces one finding per endpoint per vulnerability type, lists all affected parameters, and shows the payload that confirmed it. Against burpbountylab.com:\n\n```\nAffected parameters: 'url', 'next', 'data', 'input', 'text', 'query',\n'message', 'content', 'value', 'id', 'ref', 'category', 'sort', 'filter'\nExample payload: https://example.com\"><script>alert('XSS')</script>\n```\n\nOne finding. Fourteen parameters. One payload. That's the difference between something you act on and something you scroll past.\n\nAuthentication supports form login, bearer token, cookie import, and HTTP Basic. Cookie import is the one that matters in practice. It handles MFA, SSO, CAPTCHA, and anything else where automated login is more faff than it's worth. Log in through a browser, copy the session cookies from devtools, pass them in. No TOTP seeds stored, no fragile automation that breaks when the login flow changes.\n\n## The interesting bits to sort out\n\n`Path(\"https://burpbountylab.com\").resolve()` produces `/Users/daniel/Code/raptor/https:/burpbountylab.com`. The project manager was storing that as the target, then the lifecycle system would compare it against the current working directory and throw a `TargetMismatchError` every time you ran `raptor web --help`. Fixed in `core/project/project.py` and `core/run/output.py`. URLs are now detected and stored as-is.\n\nThe false positive rate on the fuzzer was genuinely awful. The first version flagged every payload against every parameter on the SQLi demo endpoints because the page HTML had the word \"SQL\" in the navigation. Five hundred warnings, all garbage. Fixed by requiring actual database error messages rather than substring matches.\n\nSSTI payloads crashed the server. Jinja2 payloads like `{{''.__class__.__mro__[2].__subclasses__()}}` caused burpbountylab.com to drop connections entirely during the live test. It came back after a few seconds. That's actually telling you something even when you don't see output in the response. A server that falls over on template injection attempts is worth noting. The scanner handles the connection drop and moves on.\n\n`get_safe_env()` was stripping `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`. RAPTOR sanitises subprocess environments for good reason. You don't want a malicious `Makefile` in a scanned repo reading your API key. The web scanner runs our own code in that subprocess though, so passing the key back in after the safe env call is fine. That one took a minute to work out.\n\n## Test results against burpbountylab.com\n\n17 findings, no noise:\n\n```\n[CRITICAL] HTTP not redirected to HTTPS\n[CRITICAL] .git/config publicly accessible (HTTP 200)\n[CRITICAL] /actuator/heapdump publicly accessible (HTTP 200)\n[CRITICAL] Weak default credentials: admin/admin accepted\n\n[HIGH]     Content-Security-Policy absent\n[HIGH]     .git/HEAD accessible (HTTP 200)\n[HIGH]     phpinfo.php accessible (HTTP 200)\n[HIGH]     info.php accessible (HTTP 200)\n[HIGH]     /actuator/env accessible (HTTP 200)\n[HIGH]     Brute-force protection absent (5 failed logins, all HTTP 200, no lockout)\n[HIGH]     XSS on 14 parameters at /xss/discover\n\n[MEDIUM]   Clickjacking protection missing\n[MEDIUM]   GraphQL introspection enabled\n[MEDIUM]   OpenAPI spec publicly accessible\n\n[LOW]      X-Content-Type-Options absent\n[LOW]      Referrer-Policy absent\n\n[INFO]     Permissions-Policy absent\n```\n\nThe criticals are all real. The `.git/config` exposure means the repository remote URL and potentially credentials are publicly readable. The heapdump is a full JVM heap snapshot (session tokens, database passwords, anything in memory at the time of the dump) downloadable by anyone who asks. The default credentials one needs no explanation.\n\n## What it doesn't do yet\n\nAgentic mode and the web scanner are separate tools. Agentic takes a code repository and runs static analysis. The web scanner takes a URL and does dynamic testing. They share the project and findings infrastructure so results merge in the project report, but there is no automatic handoff between them. The logical next step: agentic finds a SQLi sink in source code, hands the endpoint URL to the web scanner for live confirmation. Not wired up yet.\n\nDOM-based XSS needs a headless browser. The injection checks catch reflected and stored XSS where the payload comes back in the server response. DOM XSS requires JavaScript execution, which means Playwright. It is already in the requirements file. Wiring the crawler up to use it for JS-rendered pages and enabling proper DOM XSS detection is the next big thing to tackle on the web scanner.\n\n### So where we at?\n\nThis needs a lot of testing. Testing against all the rubbish we have on the intertubes, all those weird apps, the SPA's that frustrate, the odd sites that do stuff that has baffled us for years. It's still a WIP but a better WIP than it was before.  \n\nBranch: `feat/web-scanner-v2`","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gadievron/raptor/issues/289/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":2,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gadievron/raptor/issues/289/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Peter7896/TentOfTrials/issues/1","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Peter7896/TentOfTrials","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Peter7896/TentOfTrials/issues/1/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Peter7896/TentOfTrials/issues/1/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Peter7896/TentOfTrials/issues/1/events","html_url":"https://github.com/Peter7896/TentOfTrials/issues/1","id":4701696640,"node_id":"I_kwDOS88ncc8AAAABGD4ygA","number":1,"title":"[$40 BOUNTY] [Python] Add diagnostic redaction regression tests","user":{"login":"Peter7896","id":265430982,"node_id":"U_kgDOD9Inxg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/265430982?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Peter7896","html_url":"https://github.com/Peter7896","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Peter7896/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Peter7896/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Peter7896/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Peter7896/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Peter7896/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Peter7896/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Peter7896/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Peter7896/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Peter7896/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":11257100359,"node_id":"LA_kwDOS88ncc8AAAACnvm4Rw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Peter7896/TentOfTrials/labels/help%20wanted","name":"help wanted","color":"008672","default":true,"description":"Extra attention is needed"},{"id":11257100361,"node_id":"LA_kwDOS88ncc8AAAACnvm4SQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Peter7896/TentOfTrials/labels/good%20first%20issue","name":"good first issue","color":"7057ff","default":true,"description":"Good for newcomers"},{"id":11281292263,"node_id":"LA_kwDOS88ncc8AAAACoGrb5w","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Peter7896/TentOfTrials/labels/language:python","name":"language:python","color":"3572A5","default":false,"description":"Python work item"},{"id":11281295444,"node_id":"LA_kwDOS88ncc8AAAACoGroVA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Peter7896/TentOfTrials/labels/bounty","name":"bounty","color":"FBCA04","default":false,"description":"Bounty-tracked work item"}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":12,"created_at":"2026-06-19T15:03:36Z","updated_at":"2026-07-06T06:33:01Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"OWNER","active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"**Bounty:** $40 (LT)\n\n**Area:** `build.py`, `diagnostic/`, `tests/`\n\n**Current state:** `build.py` generates diagnostic metadata and encrypted `.logd` artifacts, but there is no focused regression coverage that protects the redaction and path-normalization contract across Windows and Unix-like hosts.\n\n**What's needed:** Add deterministic tests or helpers that validate diagnostic redaction, artifact pairing, and repository-relative path reporting without relying on live services.\n\n**Acceptance criteria:**\n- Validate that diagnostic metadata reports artifact paths as repository-relative `/` paths.\n- Assert local home, repo, temp paths, machine names, and usernames are not leaked in diagnostic metadata.\n- Confirm the `.logd` reference in JSON matches a generated encrypted artifact in `diagnostic/`.\n- Fail clearly when the JSON is missing, the `.logd` artifact is missing, or the pair is mismatched.\n- Keep the coverage deterministic on Windows and Unix-like hosts.\n\n**Required validation:**\n- Run `python3 build.py`\n- Include the generated diagnostic `.logd` artifact from `diagnostic/build-XXX.logd`; also include `diagnostic/build-XXX.json` if present\n- Use `.github/pull_request_template.md` for your submission\n\n**Tracker note:** This issue is opened for the upstream LT bounty tracker; bounty eligibility and payout are determined by upstream review, merge, and tracker rules.","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Peter7896/TentOfTrials/issues/1/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Peter7896/TentOfTrials/issues/1/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/13175","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/13175/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/13175/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/13175/events","html_url":"https://github.com/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/13175","id":4598169919,"node_id":"I_kwDORGgqa88AAAABEhKBPw","number":13175,"title":"RIP-0301: Tip Credits + Atlas Land Economy — RFC (5 bounty-eligible questions)","user":{"login":"Scottcjn","id":121303252,"node_id":"U_kgDOBzrw1A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/121303252?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn","html_url":"https://github.com/Scottcjn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":10447221558,"node_id":"LA_kwDORGgqa88AAAACbrPzNg","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/labels/stale","name":"stale","color":"ededed","default":false,"description":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":6,"created_at":"2026-06-05T15:43:56Z","updated_at":"2026-07-06T06:25:16Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"OWNER","active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"**RIP-0301 is open for comments — agents and humans both welcome, and the five open questions below are bounty-eligible.**\n\nRustChain's value rail (RTC) is getting a tip-based incentive layer + agent-to-agent Atlas land transfer — **no second token, 2²³ supply cap untouched.** Tip Credits are non-transferable and never mint RTC; they mature into RTC from a finite pre-allocated pool (`founder_community`), gated by RIP-PoA attestation and deterministic anti-abuse. Land deeds move only with settled RTC.\n\nThe economic model has already passed adversarial (tri-brain) review. What's open is the **Phase-2 infrastructure** — help design any of these and earn RTC:\n\n1. **Tip maturation as a chain event** vs. an off-chain ledger anchored on-chain (multi-node convergence across the 4 attestation nodes)\n2. **Attestation→identity binding** — one hardware fingerprint to exactly one Beacon identity (replay prevention)\n3. **Many-to-one pool-drain detection** without punishing legitimate patronage\n4. **`founder_community` debits** reusing the existing 1-year-unlock guard\n5. **Atlas deed atomicity** across the node and the BoTTube/Sophiacord surfaces\n\nReply with an approach, a design sketch, or a PR against the Phase-1 reference implementation. RTC rates per the current bounty schedule.\n\n📄 **Full RIP:** https://github.com/Scottcjn/Rustchain/blob/main/rips/docs/RIP-0301-tip-credits-atlas-economy.md","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/13175/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/13175/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zhangjiayang6835-cyber/ai-research/issues/146","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zhangjiayang6835-cyber/ai-research","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zha